<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.75 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen at 23.75 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen falling 49 basis points to 23.75 percent, and rates are also seen falling at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 10 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     24.24	    23.75		   -49  bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     24.93	    24.53		   -40  bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    25.52	    24.85		   -67  bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     26.00	    25.42		   -58  bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 EST.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom +525 7289559</p>
